p.seg:
—a formal expression
								for breaking off all political relations. Cf. V,
								80. .

]—Thuc. is arguing that in
								earlier times the spring was in 
									general use.

]—this could only apply to ἄλλοι τινές: but it is probably a note
								on οἱ Μεσσήνιοι
									καὶ ἄλλοι .

—the subject is a person;
								therefore ὑπὸ and not the dat. is
								used with the perf. pass.
